nd of reacting to that  pocket being able to take off and run  and get some yarns  so brandon staley this year  has brought a different mix obviously  than your first year what uh what has he  done with you do you think that has  helped you to where you are right now  going into week 14. justin yeah he comes  into our quarterback room all the time  just talks defense and he's got such a  great feel for defenses and especially  his own and the way they run it on on  our field and um just talking with him  and picking up so much about you know  leverage and  where the linebackers are gonna line up  and what they're trying to hide what  they're trying to disguise  we've learned a ton from him okay and  you know so much was made during your  draft period of that  uh that um  that piece of paper that you you or your  homework or what have you when you were  a kid that you grew up wanting to be a  quarterback uh in the nfl of the  chargers is this this sort of stuff  through the first year and plus that you  dreamt of i mean is this the dream that  you were you're thinking of as a kid  that you're actually realizing it just  it it's still unbelievable to realize  where i am and um you know i just have  to thank all the people that helped me  get here and i didn't do it alone and i  thank my parents my mom and my dad my  brothers my grandparents and  especially all the coaches i've had  along the way that have kind of molded  me into the quarterback that i am today  and i'm still so much  room for improvement i can get so much  better um but you know it's an honor to  be here like what seriously like what  what are you talking about room for  improvement what what what what can you  improve upon right now justin  we can always limit turnovers um you  know i can always get the ball out  quicker and  you know i think even having a better  understanding of defenses and being able  to check and go through audibles and do  all that um stuff you know i think  that's the next ste